    <briefdescription>
<para>Colours used to highlight pass and fail results in test reports. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1colours" kindref="compound">colours</ref></computeroutput> structure defines ANSI escape sequences for terminal output, enabling colour-coded highlighting of test outcomes. The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1colours_1ac3953ba58fbf322bd310c857844d17fe" kindref="member">pass</ref></computeroutput> member specifies the colour for successful results (typically green), while the <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1colours_1a7cd442bbb5af0f5d53632101d5c2eb0b" kindref="member">fail</ref></computeroutput> member specifies the colour for failed results (typically red). The <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1colours_1a42937839aa8c23e1c5482582eaf2aeb7" kindref="member">none</ref></computeroutput> member resets the colour to the terminal default.</para>
<para>By default all members are empty strings, so no escape sequences are emitted; reporters that support colours assign <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1ad59e204218aa41581652a072be0e8a8a" kindref="member">colours_red_green</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
